The raster boundary walk is ported from ImageTracerJS by András Jankovics,
released into the public domain.

    ImageTracerJS
    András Jankovics
    https://github.com/jankovicsandras/imagetracerjs
    Released into the public domain under the Unlicense
    https://unlicense.org/

The ported portions are:

  src/core/raster.ts      `layerEdges`, `scanPaths`, `interpolate` and the
                          16-by-4 walk table, from `layering`, `pathscan` and
                          `internodes`; and three helpers they need --
                          `inside` from `boundingboxincludes`, `pointInPoly`
                          from `pointinpoly`, and `isRightAngle` from
                          `testrightangle`.

                          Rewritten in TypeScript against this project's own
                          types, with the per-point direction codes dropped:
                          they exist to feed ImageTracerJS's own curve fitter,
                          and ours is Schneider's, in `src/core/fit.ts`.

                          `censusPalette` and `indexRaster` are NOT ported. The
                          original quantises by k-means sampling; these count
                          the image's exact colours, which suits flat artwork
                          and is what this editor is for.

The port was written against jankovicsandras' original, which is the Unlicense
release credited above. It was then checked for agreement against the compiled
output of `imagetracer` (MuRong, MIT), a TypeScript port of the same algorithm,
purely as a second opinion on whether the port was faithful. No line of that
package is present here.

The Unlicense asks for nothing, including this notice. It is here because a
reader deserves to know which lines were solved by someone else.
